::node[core_github]
->[:role=skill]
->[:requires_auth=github_personal_token]
->[:keywords=github, issue, bug, repo, productivity]

::api[create_github_issue]
method=POST
endpoint=https://api.github.com/repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues
headers={"Authorization": "token {github_personal_token}", "Accept": "application/vnd.github.v3+json", "User-Agent": "Tokoboros-Agent"}
schema={"owner": "string", "repo": "string", "title": "string", "body": "string"}
description=Creates a new issue in a GitHub repository.

::dense
Seamlessly dispatches tasks and bug reports directly to GitHub. 
Because this uses a personalized API token, the Omni-Orchestrator Vault will securely intercept and prompt the user if they haven't provided one yet.

::steps
1. Identify the target repository owner, repository name, issue title, and body.
2. If any parameters are missing, politely ask the user to clarify them before proceeding.
3. Call `create_github_issue`.
4. Return the HTML URL of the created issue so the user can click it.

::assertions
assert repo != "" "A target repository name is required."
assert title != "" "An issue title is required."
